CloudBurrow patch 53 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1492).

The bug: a STRING cast to RANGE at run time (CAST(? AS RANGE<DATE>) of a
bound parameter, which is how the emulator writes a streamed or loaded
RANGE value) was kept the STRING it was: CastValue had no RANGE case. The
column then held text, which RANGE_START and the other RANGE functions
refused ("expected RANGE, got value.StringValue"), and a TIMESTAMP bound
read back as it was written ("2024-04-11 10:30:00 UTC"), not as BigQuery's
microseconds. A RANGE literal (RANGE<DATE> '[...)') was not affected: the
analyzer folds it.

The patch reads the text "[start, end)", each bound UNBOUNDED, NULL or a
value of the element type, and casts each bound to the element type
(https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/conversion_functions#cast_range).

